# {{STORY_TITLE}}

## Story

As {{ROLE}} I want {{CAPABILITY}} so that {{BENEFIT}}.

## Acceptance criteria

One line per criterion, `- <key>: <criterion>`. The key is lowercase and hyphenated and
names the behaviour — never a number, because a number means nothing once the list is
reordered. Every key needs one end-user test before the build stage may run.

- {{CRITERION_KEY}}: {{OBSERVABLE_BEHAVIOUR}}

## Changed expectations

Only when the story changes behaviour the system already has: one line per expectation that no
longer holds, in the project's language — what the user or caller sees now, and what they see
after. No story ids and no file names; the plan stage finds the tests. Leave the section out when
the story only adds behaviour.

- {{WHAT_CHANGES}}

## Assumptions

Everything the story rests on that only the domain contact can confirm. Each line is a
question, answered or open — this is the asynchronous channel to the domain expert, not a
place for decisions the team took itself.

- open: {{QUESTION}}
